                "annotations": [],
                "text": "Analyse the transformation rule:\n1. In each example, there are lines of grey (5) and colorful pattern blocks.\n2. The grey lines indicate either a horizontal extent or a vertical extent to repeat the pattern along.\n   - Specifically:\n     - In example 1:\n       - Top-left: grey column at col 1 from rows 1 to 4. Block of row 1 cols 2..4 `[2, 8, 3]` is repeated vertically along rows 1..4 in cols 2..4.\n       - Bottom-right: grey row at row 9 from cols 3 to 8. Vertical column at col 8, rows 6..8 `[1, 4, 7]^T` is repeated horizontally across cols 3..8.\n     - In example 2:\n       - Grey column at col 6 from rows 1 to 7.\n       - Next to it (cols 3..5), rows 1..2 have a pattern `[[2,4,8],[7,1,3]]`. This 2-row pattern is repeated vertically down rows 1 to 7.\n     - In example 3:\n       - Grey row at row 1 from cols 1 to 8.\n       - Below it, cols 1..3, rows 2..4 have pattern of width 3. It repeats horizontally across cols 1 to 8 (wrapping/cycling horizontally).\n     - In example 4:\n       - Column 0 has grey at rows 1..6. Rows 5..6 cols 1..2 has `[[8,1],[4,7]]`. It repeats vertically along rows 1..6.\n       - Row 3 has grey at cols 4..9. Rows 1..2 cols 8..9 has `[[6,2],[3,9]]`. It repeats horizontally along cols 4..9 in rows 1..2.\n       \nSo:\n- A grey line (horizontal or vertical, color 5) defines a span.\n- An adjacent/aligned pattern of non-zero colors is extruded/tiled along the length of the grey line (either vertically if the grey line is vertical, or horizontally if the grey line is horizontal).\n- The span of the extrusion matches the coordinate range of the grey line.\n- The tiling repeats periodically if the span is larger than the pattern dimension.\n\nI am ready for the test input!",
